;; Trains at Progman St.: one train follows a cleared route through a crossover (track circuits
;; occupy/vacate in sequence, signals drop behind it, route locking releases), a second train
;; is created halted behind it, is told to be observant but is too far from the signal to
;; accelerate by itself, and follows once the route is set again; a free-will train is run past
;; a red signal on another track and is tripped by its stop; trains are halted and resumed.
;; Paths are relative to this file.
(clicktime 200 200)
(load "../../../Interlockings/Progman/progman.trk")
(say 2000 "progman: throw two switches by hand....")
(mouseright switch 9 "")
(mouseright switch 17 "")
(say 6000 "Wait for the switches...")
(say 1000 "Route: signal 2, entrance 4, exit 20")
(signal 2 "")
(signal 4 "")
(wait 500)
(signal 20 "")
(wait 8000)
(say 1000 "Train 1 enters at the south end of track 2")
(train 1 create 2693 minimizedialog)
(wait 25000)
(say 1000 "Train 2 appears behind it, halted, then is set observant")
(train 2 create 2693 halted hidedialog)
(wait 4000)
(train 2 observant)
(wait 8000)
(say 1000 "Slow train 1 down by hand")
(train 1 speed 25)
(wait 15000)
(say 1000 "A free-will train runs the red signal on track 4")
(train 3 create 4693 halted)
(train 3 freewill)
(train 3 speed 45)
(wait 3000)
(train 1 freewill)
(train 1 speed 60)
(wait 30000)
(say 1000 "Halt train 1, then let it go on")
(train 1 halt)
(wait 5000)
(train 1 observant)
(train 1 speed 40)
(wait 40000)
(say 1000 "Route again for train 2 now that the first one is clear")
(signal 2 "")
(signal 4 "")
(wait 500)
(signal 20 "")
(wait 3000)
(say 1000 "Give train 2 a push; it is too far from the signal to accelerate by itself")
(train 2 speed 20)
(wait 100000)
(say 2000 "Done.")
